              "# ZTE signed US agreement in principle to put Chinese firm back in business: Reuters, citing sources\n- ZTE has signed an agreement that would lift a U.S. Commerce Department ban on buying from U.S. suppliers, allowing the telecommunications company to get back into business.\n- ZTE ceased major operations in May and has been on life support since the seven-year ban was imposed in April, after it illegally shipped goods to Iran and North Korea.\n- Over the weekend, ZTE signed the agreement in principle drawn up by the United States, but the amended settlement agreement has not yet been signed, sources said",
